### Front‑end sign‑up flow

Edit the sign‑up form to capture the referral.

```tsx
// pages/signup.tsx (pseudo‑code)
const { ref } = useRouter();   // e.g., /signup?ref=abcd1234

const handleSignup = async (formData) => {
  const { error: signupError, user } = await supabase.auth.signUp({
    email: formData.email,
    password: formData.password,
  });

  if (signupError) {
    // show error
    return;
  }

  if (!user) return;

  // Post to our back‑end to register the referral + credits
  await fetch('/api/referral/add', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: JSON.stringify({
      newUserId: user.id,
      referrerId: ref || null,
    }),
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  });
};
```

> **Note**: `ref` comes from the URL param. If the user didn't arrive via a referral link, `referrerId` will be `null` – no credits issued.

